title: Josef Albers
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

German artist and teacher.

Studied at the [[BauHaus]], then taught there, including [[The Preliminary Course]].

When the school closed in 1933 he went to [[Black Mountain College]], and later to Yale.

Painted //Homage to the Square// for decades. Wrote //Interaction of Color//, which teaches that a color is never seen alone.

See [[Educational Model]]
